# Build artifacts (root-level binaries from go build -o ...)
/nexus3
/nexus3-agent
/bin/

# Release binaries — CD publishes linux/amd64 only (never committed).
# dist/ held nexus3-darwin-arm64 until 2026-08-21; darwin was removed because
# internal/core/builder/builderimage is linux-only (no darwin build stubs).
/dist/

# Go test and coverage output
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Development metadata
.claude/
# ...except repo-scoped skills, which describe how this repo is developed and
# are useless to a collaborator if they do not survive a clone.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# ...but not eval scratch output, which is throwaway run artefacts.
.claude/skills/*-workspace/
.codegraph/
.groundwork/

# Intermediate prototypes and plans
.scratch/
/buildorca

# Docs site build artifacts (VitePress). The Markdown under docs/site is the
# source; node_modules and the rendered output are never committed.
docs/site/node_modules/
docs/site/.vitepress/dist/
docs/site/.vitepress/cache/
__pycache__/

# repro harness generated blobs and build logs (~450 MB of binary test files
# and per-run log files). run.sh and any Containerfile templates remain tracked.
# These paths are produced by internal/test/repro/run.sh and must not be committed.
internal/test/repro/logs/
internal/test/repro/workspace/
internal/test/repro/workspace_pressure_*/

# test leakage: netns control sockets + auth tokens written relative to CWD
internal/core/driver/cloudhypervisor/netns-control/

# slice-sandbox agent reports: an in-guest agent writes its narrative report
# here because the pane transcript can become unreachable (SKILL.md mode 6).
# It is a working artefact of one slice, never part of the tree.
.slice-report.md
